# Node
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Secrets & cryptographic key material
# This project implements a verifiable trust layer for AI agents (identity,
# credentials, scoped authority) — real private keys, signing keys, and
# credential secrets WILL be generated and used locally during development.
# None of that material may ever be committed, even accidentally.
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jwk
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*.crt.key

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor junk
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Vercel
.vercel

# Next.js-generated agent notes
# AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md at the repo root are rewritten by `next dev` /
# `next build` itself (see node_modules/next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js)
# to document Next 16 breaking changes for coding agents. They are
# machine-generated, agent-advisory scratch notes, not project content —
# they regenerate on every build, so tracking them just adds churn to a
# public repo judges will read. They stay on disk (Next keeps rewriting
# them); they are just no longer tracked in git.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
